  "title": "10-minute home cardio workout",
  "creator": "NHS",
  "description": "Four bodyweight cardio moves, two sets of each, from the old NHS Fitness Studio 10-minute series. It is meant to raise the heart rate at home with no kit; each set is 15 to 24 reps and one exercise can be swapped for 60 seconds of skipping. Swap star jumps for squats or do burpees without the push-up position to make it easier. Warm up first with the NHS 6-minute warm-up (nhs-6-min-warm-up) and finish with the 5-minute stretch (nhs-5-min-cool-down-stretch).",
